{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-220346",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To express the equation of the parabola in vertex form, we need to complete the square. \n\nFirst, we take out a factor of $5$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-10x+15 & =5({x}^{2}-2x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+3 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot x+3 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot x+{1}^{2}-{1}^{2}+3 & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot x+{1}^{2})-{1}^{2}+3 & = \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}+3 & = \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+3 & = \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5({x}^{2}-2x+3) & = \\\\ 5((x-1)^{2}+2) & = \\\\ 5(x-1)^{2}+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, expressed in vertex form, the equation of the parabola is $y=5(x-1)^{2}+10.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
